5. Overall Architectural Principle

The future platform should provide a scalable, reusable enterprise foundation where applications share common data, entities, permissions, relationships, work items, notifications, files, and agent capabilities wherever practical.

The guiding principle is:

Build the foundation once, establish clear guardrails, avoid redundant backend implementations, and allow future applications to build on the same platform without breaking the underlying architecture.
